     "id": "av",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "−7 ÷ 2 = −3.5, and the shift gave −4: an arithmetic right shift divides by 2 and rounds down (towards −∞), not towards zero.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "av",
     "set": {
      "text": "−4 = ⌊−3.5⌋"
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "A logical shift right fills the top with 0 instead. 01111100 = 124: fine for unsigned numbers, wrong for negative ones.",
